<%- include("templates/publicpages_header", {
  title: "BeeWilder | Welcome"
}) %>

<main class="bw-page">
  <header class="bw-hero d-flex align-items-center">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row align-items-center g-5">
        <div class="col-lg-6">

          <h1 class="bw-title">
            Explore plants with <span>curiosity</span>, not guesswork.
          </h1>

          <p class="bw-copy mt-4">
            BeeWilder is a safety-first plant discovery app.
            Scan or upload a plant photo, compare possible matches, review
            confidence and risk notes, save discoveries, explore a seasonal
            plant map, and build plant knowledge through games.
          </p>

          <div class="d-flex flex-column flex-sm-row gap-3 mt-4">
            <a class="btn bw-btn-primary btn-lg px-4" href="/signup">
              Join us!
            </a>

            <a class="btn bw-btn-outline btn-lg px-4" href="/login">
              Log in
            </a>
          </div>

          <div class="bw-warning bw-danger-warning mt-4">
            <div class="d-flex gap-3">
              <span class="warning-icon">!</span>
              <p class="mb-0">
                <strong>Safety first.</strong>
                BeeWilder is a learning and decision-support tool. Never eat,
                touch, or prepare a wild plant based on one scan alone.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-lg-5 offset-lg-1">
          <div class="bw-notebook field-card-lines p-4">
            <div
              class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center mb-4"
            >
              <span class="bw-tag">Procedure</span>
            </div>

            <h2 class="h3 fw-black mb-3">A safer first step outdoors.</h2>

            <div class="row g-3">
              <div class="col-6">
                <div class="bw-card h-100">
                  <span class="bw-icon">01</span>
                  <h3 class="h6 fw-bold">Scan</h3>
                  <p class="small mb-0">
                    Capture a plant photo or upload one from your device.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="col-6">
                <div class="bw-card h-100">
                  <span class="bw-icon">02</span>
                  <h3 class="h6 fw-bold">Check</h3>
                  <p class="small mb-0">
                    Review confidence, warnings, and possible lookalikes.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="col-6">
                <div class="bw-card h-100">
                  <span class="bw-icon">03</span>
                  <h3 class="h6 fw-bold">Save</h3>
                  <p class="small mb-0">
                    Store useful discoveries in your personal plant journal.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="col-6">
                <div class="bw-card h-100">
                  <span class="bw-icon">04</span>
                  <h3 class="h6 fw-bold">Learn</h3>
                  <p class="small mb-0">
                    Explore maps, encyclopedia entries, and plant games.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <hr>

            <p class="small text-muted mb-0">
              Designed for students, hikers, foragers, and beginners who want
              clearer plant information before making outdoor decisions.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section id="features" class="bw-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row align-items-end mb-4">
        <div class="col-lg-7">
          <h2 class="bw-section-title">
            What BeeWilder does
          </h2>
        </div>

        <div class="col-lg-5">
          <p class="bw-copy mb-0">
            BeeWilder does not replace expert judgement. It organizes plant
            information into a clearer path, so users can slow down, compare,
            learn, and avoid risky assumptions.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="row g-4">
        <div class="col-md-6 col-xl-3">
          <article class="bw-card h-100">
            <span class="bw-icon">📷</span>
            <h3 class="h5 fw-bold">Plant scan</h3>
            <p class="mb-0">
              Scan or upload a plant photo and receive possible plant matches
              with readable confidence guidance.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-6 col-xl-3">
          <article class="bw-card h-100">
            <span class="bw-icon">⚠</span>
            <h3 class="h5 fw-bold">Risk notes</h3>
            <p class="mb-0">
              See warnings, lookalike reminders, ripeness notes, and basic
              preparation cautions before trusting a result.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-6 col-xl-3">
          <article class="bw-card h-100">
            <span class="bw-icon">🗺</span>
            <h3 class="h5 fw-bold">Plant map</h3>
            <p class="mb-0">
              Explore nearby plant sightings, map pins, seasonal availability,
              and location-based plant information.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-6 col-xl-3">
          <article class="bw-card h-100">
            <span class="bw-icon">🌿</span>
            <h3 class="h5 fw-bold">My Plants</h3>
            <p class="mb-0">
              Save discoveries into a personal field journal and filter by
              plant type, safety level, location, or season.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="safety" class="bw-section pt-0">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row g-4 align-items-stretch">
        <div class="col-lg-5">
          <div class="bw-warning h-100">
            <p class="bw-kicker">Safety warning</p>
            <h2 class="h3 fw-bold">BeeWilder helps you ask better questions.</h2>
            <p>
              It does not tell you something is safe to eat with certainty.
              Users should always verify with trusted sources, local field
              guides, knowledgeable people, and official safety information.
            </p>
            <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
              <span class="bw-tag danger">Do not rely on one scan</span>
              <span class="bw-tag warn">Check lookalikes</span>
              <span class="bw-tag">Save notes</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-lg-7">
          <div class="accordion bw-accordion" id="safetyAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-item">
              <h2 class="accordion-header">
                <button
                  class="accordion-button"
                  type="button"
                  data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                  data-bs-target="#safetyOne"
                  aria-expanded="true"
                  aria-controls="safetyOne"
                >
                  Why the app shows warnings
                </button>
              </h2>

              <div
                id="safetyOne"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse show"
                data-bs-parent="#safetyAccordion"
              >
                <div class="accordion-body">
                  Many edible plants have unsafe lookalikes. BeeWilder surfaces
                  risk notes and confidence language so users know when to slow
                  down instead of assuming a result is correct.
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordion-item">
              <h2 class="accordion-header">
                <button
                  class="accordion-button collapsed"
                  type="button"
                  data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                  data-bs-target="#safetyTwo"
                  aria-expanded="false"
                  aria-controls="safetyTwo"
                >
                  What to verify before handling a plant
                </button>
              </h2>

              <div
                id="safetyTwo"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                data-bs-parent="#safetyAccordion"
              >
                <div class="accordion-body">
                  Compare leaf shape, stem texture, growth pattern, location,
                  season, plant condition, and reliable identification sources.
                  When unsure, leave the plant alone.
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordion-item">
              <h2 class="accordion-header">
                <button
                  class="accordion-button collapsed"
                  type="button"
                  data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                  data-bs-target="#safetyThree"
                  aria-expanded="false"
                  aria-controls="safetyThree"
                >
                  What BeeWilder is best used for
                </button>
              </h2>

              <div
                id="safetyThree"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                data-bs-parent="#safetyAccordion"
              >
                <div class="accordion-body">
                  BeeWilder is best for learning, organizing discoveries,
                  comparing possible matches, and exploring seasonal plant
                  information. It is not a substitute for expert identification.
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="app-sections" class="bw-section pt-0">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row g-4 align-items-center">
        <div class="col-lg-5">
          <h2 class="bw-section-title">
            What joining us allows you to do!
          </h2>
        </div>

        <div class="col-lg-7">
          <div class="bw-tab-shell p-3">
            <ul
              class="nav nav-pills bw-tabs gap-2 mb-3"
              id="featureTabs"
              role="tablist"
            >
              <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                <button
                  class="nav-link active"
                  data-bs-toggle="pill"
                  data-bs-target="#scanTab"
                  type="button"
                  role="tab"
                >
                  Scan
                </button>
              </li>

              <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                <button
                  class="nav-link"
                  data-bs-toggle="pill"
                  data-bs-target="#mapTab"
                  type="button"
                  role="tab"
                >
                  Map
                </button>
              </li>

              <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                <button
                  class="nav-link"
                  data-bs-toggle="pill"
                  data-bs-target="#libraryTab"
                  type="button"
                  role="tab"
                >
                  Library
                </button>
              </li>

              <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                <button
                  class="nav-link"
                  data-bs-toggle="pill"
                  data-bs-target="#learnTab"
                  type="button"
                  role="tab"
                >
                  Learn
                </button>
              </li>
            </ul>

            <div class="tab-content">
              <div class="tab-pane fade show active" id="scanTab" role="tabpanel">
                <h3 class="h5 fw-bold">Plant Scan</h3>
                <p class="mb-0">
                  The scan feature is the starting point for possible plant
                  identification, confidence scoring, and safety guidance.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="tab-pane fade" id="mapTab" role="tabpanel">
                <h3 class="h5 fw-bold">Plant Map</h3>
                <p class="mb-0">
                  The map helps users explore nearby plant sightings and learn
                  what may be present or in season around them.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="tab-pane fade" id="libraryTab" role="tabpanel">
                <h3 class="h5 fw-bold">My Plants and Encyclopedia</h3>
                <p class="mb-0">
                  My Plants stores personal discoveries, while the encyclopedia
                  gives users a broader reference point for known plants.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="tab-pane fade" id="learnTab" role="tabpanel">
                <h3 class="h5 fw-bold">Plant Games</h3>
                <p class="mb-0">
                  Games turn plant identification into practice, helping users
                  build confidence through repetition and feedback.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="row g-4 mt-4">
        <div class="col-md-4">
          <article class="bw-card h-100">
            <h3 class="h5 fw-bold">For beginners</h3>
            <p class="mb-0">
              Clear labels, step-by-step guidance, and safety-first wording
              reduce confusion for first-time users.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-4">
          <article class="bw-card h-100">
            <h3 class="h5 fw-bold">For outdoor users</h3>
            <p class="mb-0">
              The map helps hikers, students, and foragers learn
              what is around them without assuming it is safe to consume.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-4">
          <article class="bw-card h-100">
            <h3 class="h5 fw-bold">For returning users</h3>
            <p class="mb-0">
              Saved plants, profile tools, settings, and game progress support
              repeat learning over time.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="faq" class="bw-section pt-0">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="bw-panel">
        <div class="row g-4 align-items-center">
          <div class="col-lg-7">
            <p class="bw-kicker">Purpose and goal</p>
            <h2 class="bw-section-title">
              BeeWilder exists to make plant discovery more responsible.
            </h2>
            <p class="bw-copy mb-0">
              The goal is not to encourage risky foraging. The goal is to make
              outdoor learning more structured by combining scanning, safety
              prompts, map context, saved observations, encyclopedia reference,
              and practice games in one app.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="col-lg-5">
            <div class="bw-metric-grid">
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<%- include("templates/publicpages_footer") %>
